---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ThemeDial from '../components/ThemeDial.astro';
import WorkList from '../components/WorkList.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import BrandLogo from '../components/BrandLogo.astro';
---
<BaseLayout>
  <section class="intro-section" aria-labelledby="hello">
    <div class="home-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Well, hello there <span aria-hidden="true">✳</span></p><h1 id="hello">I'm Gabby<span class="heading-dot">.</span></h1></div>
      <ThemeDial />
    </div>
    <div class="intro-copy">
      <p>I’m a <span class="inline-emphasis"><span aria-hidden="true">👩🏻‍💻</span> software engineer</span>, cat mom to Nori and Kimchi, collector of hobbies, and a curious lifelong learner. I live in San Francisco, but New England will always feel like home.</p>
      <p>These days, I’m helping people find meaningful work training next-gen AI models as a founding engineer at <a class="inline-link sage-link brand-name" href="https://joinhandshake.com/ai"><BrandLogo name="handshake" /> Handshake AI</a>, tinkering on some (still top-secret) side projects, and finding time to <a class="inline-link sage-link" href="/garden/"><Icon name="plant" /> tend to my digital garden</a>.</p>
      <p>Before Handshake, I grew from an engineering apprentice into a senior software engineer at <a class="inline-link brand-name" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LinkedIn"><BrandLogo name="linkedin" /> LinkedIn</a>. I learned to code at <a class="inline-link brand-name" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hack_Reactor"><BrandLogo name="hack-reactor" /> Hack Reactor</a>, where I later taught as a Software Engineer in Residence. Some of the work I’m proudest of has been making software more accessible and helping other engineers from nontraditional backgrounds find their footing.</p>
      <p>My path into tech had a few side quests. After studying political science and leadership studies at <a class="inline-link brand-name" href="https://www.williams.edu/"><BrandLogo name="williams" /> Williams College</a>, I worked as a business analyst at a language-learning startup, a community marketer at a values-driven solar company in Vermont, and an independent SAT tutor.</p>
      <p>Away from work, you might find me tinkering with my <span class="inline-emphasis"><Icon name="coffee" /> espresso setup</span>, lost in a good book, or spelunking down a Wikipedia rabbit hole. I love journaling and collecting stationery, trying my hand at photography around San Francisco, and cooking for friends and family—with a cozy game or some quality cat time in between.</p>
      <p>This is my little home on the internet. A place for <a class="inline-link rose-link" href="/blog/"><Icon name="notebook" /> words</a>, <a class="inline-link sage-link" href="/garden/"><Icon name="flower" /> growing things</a>, and whatever comes next. Make yourself at home.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="quiet-link now-link" href="/now/"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> What I'm up to now <Icon name="right" /></a>
  </section>
  <section class="work-section" aria-labelledby="work-heading">
    <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="work-heading">Work</h2><a href="/resume/" class="quiet-link">The longer version <Icon name="arrow" /></a></div>
    <WorkList />
  </section>
  <aside class="garden-invitation"><Icon name="plant" /><p>There's a little more down the garden path.<br /><a href="/garden/">Take a look around <Icon name="right" /></a></p><span aria-hidden="true" class="garden-asterisk">✳</span></aside>
</BaseLayout>
